Like this one.  It's the classic tradeoff.

As far as armor class goes, any dragon scale mail that you can come
by without wishing is worth using.  Per AC point it's lighter than
any other mail and it starts out with more AC.  But each one confers
an intrinsic and dragons always leave corpses.  Eating the dragon
corpse gives you the intrinsic most of the time in several cases.

Cold/fire/poison/shock/sleep resistance can be gotten from other
corpses but if you don't have one by the time you kill your first
dragon of the matching color it is well worth eating the corpse to
get that intrinsic and not need the mail for anything but AC.

Disintigration intrinsic is so worthwhile it's worth teleporting
around or waiting on another level until you aren't satiated before
facing the dragon so you can eat it.  It's the only corpse that gives
disintigration resistance but eating beats wearing.

Acid isn't that strong a weapon and you can't get acid resistance
by eating a yellow dragon.

That leaves the classic tradeoff of silver versus grey.  Eating does
not work for either.  Both convey intrinsics so valuable they are
worth having redundantly if you conveniently can.  The Samurai quest
artifact conveys luck, which is another intrinsic worth having
redundantly if you can, but neither reflection nor MR.

MR comes from [GDSM, [oMR or quest artifacts from other classes.
That's a narrow list.  Reflection comes from [SDSM, "oR, [oR or
quest artifacts from other classes.  A Samurai CAN have both
redundant with [GDSM + [oMR + "oR + [oR but that gives up other
valuable options.  No #twoweapon so goodbye shield.  No other good
amulets so goodbye amulet.

Without those two items, [SDSM + [oMR give both without being
redundant.  It keeps the most possible options open.  And that's why
many prefer it.  But the cost is the other cloaks.  Which is why
the preference isn't even close to unanymous.

Worse is the short, medium and long views.  In the short view
reflection makes the mines doable favoring SDSM.  In the medium
view there's a 50-50 chance of the amulet in Sokoban and no
guaranteed [oMR anywhere favoring GDSM.  This is why I will always
finish Sokoban before rubbing any magic lamp.  Getting the amulet
makes chosing GDSM easier and it's good enough to finish with.

